Read Deflate64 (zip method 9) entries with Microsoft's InflateLib.

Issue: https://github.com/zippy1981/windows-nano-baseimages/issues/7
Upstream: libarchive has no Deflate64 decoder (libarchive/libarchive#2325, #2867).
This is a port of the open upstream PR https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive/pull/2806
(commit bc88f324db31, by the InflateLib authors) to libarchive 3.8.11, without its tests, vcpkg
and autoconf changes. It adds ENABLE_INFLATELIB (off by default), finds inflatelib with
find_package(inflatelib CONFIG), and decodes method 9 in the seekable and streaming zip readers,
in symlink targets and in Mac metadata, the same way method 8 is decoded with zlib.
Two changes from the PR: the Mac metadata path sets ret = ARCHIVE_FATAL on a decode error (as
3.8.11's Deflate path does), and CreatePkgConfigFile.cmake writes the imported target
inflatelib::inflatelib as -linflatelib instead of -linflatelib::inflatelib.

InflateLib: https://github.com/microsoft/inflatelib (MIT), built by scripts/build-libarchive.sh.

